{"id":"000W0B","title":"24","author":"StatisticallyYes","solvedCount":1,"difficulty":3,"rating":"N/A","firstSeen":"2026-11-13T17:50:10+00:00","posted":"Heute, 15:42 Uhr","rules":"I've previously made a puzzle called Sums and Products with a similar rule set. But it was hard to make multiplication cages without it being obvious from the totals. So I decided to make one where all the cages have the same total. I had to scrap the yin and yang idea to accomplish it, but I'm really happy with the result. I hope you enjoy it too!\n\nRules\n\nNormal sudoku rules apply: each row, column, and box must contain the digits 1 to 9 without repeats.\n\nFor each cage, the number in the top left corner is the total. For some cages, the total is the sum of all the digits in the cage. For the others, it is the product of the digits. Digits cannot repeat in cages of either type.\n\nThe 4 cells with diamonds act similar to another cage. The total can either be a product or a sum of the 4 numbers. The total is 24. Unlike in cages, there may (or may not) be repeats.\n\nLink to sudokupad","solutionCode":"Row 5 (left to right, no spaces)","tags":["Sudoku","Produkte","Killer (Variante)"],"links":[{"url":"https://sudokupad.app/b3rghi9dsv","kind":"sudokupad"}],"data":"","error":null,"settings":{},"link":"https://sudokupad.app/b3rghi9dsv","linkKind":"sudokupad","summary":{"format":"scl","decoded":true,"rows":9,"cols":9,"cages":21,"hasSolution":true,"features":["underlays"]},"attempts":0,"fetched":"2026-11-13T17:50:10+00:00"}